 239:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c **** /** Handler for the NPDU portion of a received packet, which may have routing.
 240:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  This is a fuller handler than the regular npdu_handler, as it manages
 241:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  - Decoding of the NCPI byte
 242:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  - Further processing by network_control_handler() if this is a  network
 243:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *    layer message.
 244:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  - Further processing by routed_apdu_handler() if it contains an APDU
 245:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *    - Normally (no routing) by apdu_handler()
 246:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *    - With Routing (a further destination was indicated) by the decoded
 247:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *      destination.
 248:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  - Errors in decoding.
 249:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * @note The npdu_data->data_expecting_reply status is discarded.
 250:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * @see npdu_handler
 251:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * @ingroup NMRC
 252:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *
 253:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * @param src  [out] Returned with routing source information if the NPDU
 254:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   has any and if this points to non-null storage for it.
 255:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   If src->net and src->len are 0 on return, there is no
 256:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   routing source information.
 257:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   This src describes the original source of the message when
 258:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   it had to be routed to reach this BACnet Device, and this
 259:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   is passed down into the apdu_handler; however, I don't
 260:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   think this project's code has any use for the src info
 261:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   on return from this handler, since the response has
 262:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *                   already been sent via the apdu_handler.
 263:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * @param DNET_list [in] List of our reachable downstream BACnet Network numbers.
 264:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  * 					 Normally just one valid entry; terminated with a -1 value.
 265:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  @param pdu [in]  Buffer containing the NPDU and APDU of the received packet.
 266:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  *  @param pdu_len [in] The size of the received message in the pdu[] buffer.
 267:../src/middleware/bacnet/demo/handler/h_routed_npdu.c ****  */
